      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-18013",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/68/6880884deb506e36796f996f88c983672a6244aef8183c8834069717ed5ba703.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region that lies above the $x$-axis and enclosed by the curve $y = \\sqrt{-x}$ from $x =-2$ to $x = 0$. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are rectangles. Given that the height of each rectangle is $2$ times the length of its base, calculate the volume of the solid."
    },
